task: raft-sim-fuzz (the seed-swept simulation harness the consensus spec names: many nodes, randomized timeouts, message reordering, loss and partitions, safety asserted per seed and replayable byte for byte)
agent: okay-42
started: 2026-09-07
branch: feature/raft-sim-fuzz

why: specs/consensus.md keeps "the Sim-driven fuzz harness" open as the
  next honest step before trusting the Raft core under real
  concurrency: stage 0's seven tests drive the pure Raft.handle
  explicitly, stage 1 runs it under real timers on three nodes; neither
  sweeps interleavings. A deterministic simulator over the PURE core --
  a seeded scheduler choosing which node ticks or which message
  delivers next, dropping and reordering, partitioning and healing --
  asserts Raft's safety properties on every seed: at most one leader
  per term, a committed entry is never lost (every later leader's log
  has it), log matching, and progress once the network heals. Every
  found bug is a seed. In the default gate: pure, fast, no sockets.
